      ],
      "image": "assets/images/205747/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place ground beef into a large bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/cSTwFleesykqbxLNMAhxdRYB5kk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/205747-Homemade-Beef-Breakfast-Sausage-Patties-ddmfs-4x3-step-02-5b4eead104bf40ddb1c038e3f81c7b63.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/205747/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir brown sugar, sage, salt, basil, black pepper, onion powder, marjoram, and red pepper flakes together in a small bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/5lhDROLdKag32nUZF0dW2ILUrpc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/205747-Homemade-Beef-Breakfast-Sausage-Patties-ddmfs-4x3-step-03-f5ca7cfab771445d803d32ae9b5b7940.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/205747/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sprinkle over beef and use your hands to mix until evenly distributed. Cover and refrigerate until flavors have blended, about 24 hours.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Bs1nizSLPJa7wD3x1n_8AcJHmrM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/205747-Homemade-Beef-Breakfast-Sausage-Patties-ddmfs-4x3-step-05-2fd3f16e31154c3886c74d2571e92619.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/205747/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide beef mixture into 8 patties.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/tESBeZBbD_QgQz-30JPIwh82I9U=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/205747-Homemade-Beef-Breakfast-Sausage-Patties-ddmfs-4x3-step-07-8e1c1c2382f541cf8cade41fa71a2e14.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/205747/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat a large nonstick skillet over medium heat. Working in batches, cook patties in the hot skillet until firm and no longer pink in the center, 5 to 7 minutes per side. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 160 degrees F (70 degrees C).",
